---
import Legal from '../../components/Legal.astro';
---
<Legal
  site="academy"
  title="Privacy Policy — Tisvia Marketing Academy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Tisvia Marketing Academy collects, uses and protects student information."
  updated="10 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information Tisvia Marketing Academy collects from students and
    enquirers, why, and what we do with it.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Nothing.</strong> This site has no enrolment form, no login, no advertising pixel and no
    analytics script. It sets no cookies. Nothing you do on the page is recorded by us.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel's servers process the standard request
    information needed to deliver a page — your IP address, the page requested, your browser type
    and the time of the request. We do not use this for tracking or profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect when you enquire</h2>
  <p>
    Enrolment happens over WhatsApp, email or a phone call. We receive whatever you send:
    typically your name, phone number, email address, and what you do now.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect when you enrol</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, phone number and email address, for the class group and the session links.</li>
    <li>Payment records for the course fee.</li>
    <li>The assignments you submit and your final assessment, so we can give feedback and issue
      the certificate.</li>
    <li>Your participation in the live sessions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Session recordings</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Every live session is recorded.</strong> If your microphone or camera is on, or you ask
    a question in the session, you will be in that recording. Recordings are shared with the
    students of that batch. If you would rather not appear, keep your camera and microphone off and
    ask your questions in the chat.
  </p>

  <h2>The WhatsApp class group</h2>
  <p>
    The course runs alongside a WhatsApp group. Everyone in the group can see your phone number and
    your display name. Join only if you are comfortable with that; tell us if you would rather
    receive the material by email instead.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To enrol you, send session links and run the course.</li>
    <li>To mark your assignments and give individual feedback.</li>
    <li>To issue your Certificate of Completion.</li>
    <li>To tell you about the next batch or follow-up sessions, if you ask us to.</li>
    <li>To keep the accounting records the law requires.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information, and we do not share it with anyone for their own marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    Running an online course means using other companies' tools — Zoom or a similar platform for
    the live sessions, WhatsApp for the class group, email, cloud storage for recordings and
    materials, and a payment provider for the fee. Each handles data under its own privacy policy,
    and we use only what the course requires.
  </p>
  <p>
    Fellow students in your batch see your name and, in the class group, your phone number.
  </p>

  <h2>Testimonials</h2>
  <p>
    We sometimes show messages students have sent us. We remove phone numbers before publishing. If
    your message is on our site and you want it taken down, email us and we will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not lead to enrolment are kept for up to two years. Student records,
    assignments and certificate records are kept for up to three years so we can re-issue a
    certificate if you need one. Payment records are kept as long as tax law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable care with your information and limit access to the people running the
    course. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee
    absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask us to delete it, as
    far as the law allows us to. Write to the email address below and we will respond within 30
    days. You can leave the WhatsApp group at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>
    The course is for adults. Students under 18 need a parent or guardian to enrol on their behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The date at the top of the page shows when it last changed.
  </p>
</Legal>
